== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Redstone ore must be mined with an [[iron pickaxe]] or higher to drop [[redstone dust]]. When mined, it drops 4&ndash;5 redstone dust. It is affected by the [[Fortune]] enchantment, dropping 4-6, 4-7, or 4-8 redstone respectively with Fortune I, II, and III (averaging at 6 redstone dust with Fortune level 3<ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20210311215700/https://imgur.com/a/UnIGPKn</ref><ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20230509054859/https://imgur.com/a/GirweJL</ref>). If mined with [[Silk Touch]], it drops itself instead of redstone dust.
{{Breaking row
|Redstone Ore;Deepslate Redstone Ore
|link = none; none
|Pickaxe; Pickaxe
|Iron; Iron
|drop=0; 0}}

=== Natural generation ===
{{see also|Ore (feature)}}
Redstone ore can generate in the [[Overworld]] in the form of ore features. Redstone ore generates in two batches per chunk. The first batch attempts to generate 4 times per chunk, in blobs of 0&ndash;10, evenly from levels -64 to 15. The second batch attempts to generate 8 times per chunk, in blobs of 0&ndash;10, from levels -63 to -32, being more common the lower the elevation.

Redstone ore can replace [[stone]], [[andesite]], [[diorite]], [[granite]], [[tuff]], and [[deepslate]]. Any redstone ore that replaces tuff below Y=0 or deepslate becomes deepslate redstone ore.

Unlike most ores, redstone ore does not generate less when exposed to air.

{{Block distribution}}

== Usage ==
The primary usage of redstone ore is to [[#Breaking|mine]] it for [[redstone dust]].
=== Lit redstone ore ===
[[File:Redstone Ore lit.gif|thumb|A redstone ore that glows and emits particles in the dark]]
Lit redstone ore is a block state of redstone ore or deepslate redstone ore. It produces the [[light level]] of 9 and emits bright red powered redstone particles. With the "Render Dragon Features for Creators" [[experiment]], lit redstone ore has a [[light color]] of {{color|#c32c1f}}.

Redstone ore enters this state instantly when a player interacts with it by pressing either the {{control|break}} or the {{control|use}} control, or when an entity touches it on the top side. There are some exceptions, including [[sneaking]] players, projectiles, [[shulker]]s, and the [[ender dragon]]. This effect continues until the redstone ore block receives a [[random tick]] (averaging 68.27 seconds). This effect does not actually produce redstone power, but the block changes can be detected with an [[observer]].

Subsequent interactions on a redstone ore block causes it to emit an extra burst of particles per interaction.

Unlike most other [[interactable blocks]], clicking on a redstone ore with a block, in addition to emitting particles and entering lit mode, also attempts place the block. {{IN|JE}} if the block next to the ore in the clicked direction is replaceable (like air or water), but the placed block fails (because it needs some support, for example), the redstone ore enters lit mode, but the player's hand does not move.{{more info|What happens in BE?}}

