== Trivia ==
* In the real world, {{w|diorite}} comes from underground {{w|magma chamber}}s that turned cold. Diorite usually has a salt & pepper appearance.
** {{w|Andesite}} is diorite's above-ground equivalent: The two rocks come from the same kind of {{w|magma}}, but andesite forms in {{w|lava flow}}s. Its fast cooling is what makes it look smoother than diorite.
** {{w|Granite}} is another magma chamber rock, but it's made of more quartz crystals. That is why in ''Minecraft'', granite can be crafted by combining diorite and [[nether quartz]].
* In the real world, diorite is an extremely hard rock and is difficult to carve and work with.
* In ''[[Minecraft: Story Mode]]'', Reuben's grave on Episode 4 is made out of diorite and a new stair variant of it which cannot be found in ''[[Minecraft]]'' until the [[Village & Pillage]] update, which was announced roughly 3 years after Episode 4. It is unknown whether diorite slabs are present.

